# EXP-0072 R3 menu judder A/B (same build 1a6bfe90)
# user: 「两者都抖，只有stop了才不抖」
# interpretation: the A/B separated the injection, not the upscaler.

## What the two "modes" actually were

# - "Suppress TAAU draw" ON : the TAAU quad is skipped, our DLSS writes arg10.
# - "Restore TAAU draw" OFF: the TAAU quad runs, but stage B is still armed, so our
#   injected list writes the DLSS output into arg10 AFTER it. The user still sees DLSS.
# - "Stop" (Stop arg10)   : injection off, arg10Solid off -> TAAU is the only writer.
# => "both judder" = both were DLSS; "only stop is smooth" = pure TAAU is smooth.
# The judder therefore comes from our DLSS -> arg10 path, not from the menu itself and
# not from skipping the TAAU draw.

